  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed dormers, by reason of their scale, siting and design, appear as dominant and incongruous additions to the roofslope which cause harm to the character and appearance of the host property and conservation area, \r\ncontrary to policies D1 (Design) and D2 (Heritage) of the Camden Local Plan (2017).\r\n",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed boundary treatment, by reason of its design and materials, would be incongruous addition and would therefore be harmful to the character and appearance of the host building, the streetscene, and wider Camden Square Conservation Area, contrary to policies D1 (Design) and D2 (Heritage) of the Camden Local Plan 2017.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed outbuilding by reason of its siting, scale and design, would dominate the rear garden of the host property and detract from the open setting of neighbouring gardens, failing to appear as a subordinate garden addition and detracting from the  character and appearance of Camden Square Conservation area, contrary to Policies A1 (Managing the impact of development), D1 (Design) and D2 (Heritage) of the Camden Local Plan 2017.",
    "Reason : 4 - In the absence of an adequate Tree Survey and Arboricultural Impact Assessment the applicant has failed to demonstrate that the proposed outbuilding would not cause unacceptable harm to trees or on site habitats, contrary to policy A3 (Biodiversity) of the London Borough of Camden Local Plan 2017."
  ],
